    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8a23b02_41750051",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 262,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-26T17:23:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good callout - so, if a shader *only* uses dynamic samplers, that can be indicated with an empty shader node data span. \n\nHowever, if a shader uses, say, both a dynamic and immutable sampler (I don\u0027t think this is possible to encounter right now, and I don\u0027t foresee it being all that likely, but theoretically)... then we would have to add a \"0\" to indicate \"at this binding index, there\u0027s a regular sampler\", followed by the immutable sampler description. If we only had the latter with no \"0\" for the dynamic sampler, then we would not know which binding index that sampler should be at.\n\nLMK if that makes sense or if you think encountering this scenario is impossible and we needn\u0027t worry about it, if the comment can be more clear, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "8f481076_9187af40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 262,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 262,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "a20ff7afeac38833e0bea33358316f07d2d9b078",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99f23a83_fbdd54bd",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 262,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-26T18:20:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting, I was thinking we were going to be filling out these outDescs for every shader with samplers regardless what combination of dynamic or immutable samples it may have. And that the current checks for null in the code were all related to not having this fully plumbed yet. So I guess it is true that we will only fill out one of the Desc structs if there is a least 1 immutable sampler? Would anything break today if we filled out a desc array of all dynamic samplers? If we think the empty array is a nice optimization to have then that is fine to keep.\n\nRegardless of that, if we are in this code we do have data. Thus I still think the comment can be more exact and avoid things like \"may\" which is a little ambiguous if things are optional or not.",
      "parentUuid": "d8a23b02_41750051",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 262,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 262,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "a20ff7afeac38833e0bea33358316f07d2d9b078",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff6b1dfa_8e490329",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ContextUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 262,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-30T16:59:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think a useful callout to make in this comment is that this is specifically referring to a shader *snippet* that has multiple textures, which could then be a mix of immutable samplers and dynamic samplers, e.g. the YUV snippets.\n\nRight now if they have any immutable sampler, they push back the sampler description for every texture into a node\u0027s data vs. somehow encoding a plane index + sampler description. I definitely had forgotten that this case needed to be handled here and started to write up just having it simplified to push back one `SamplerDesc`.\n\nWe could remove the check against `0` and take it into account when calculating `samplerDataLength \u003d 1`, but we\u0027d also need to make sure that when we filled out the nodes sampler descriptions that they were using a default dynamic sampler and not their actual dynamic sampler to avoid creating a new paint key. Since that requirement still exists where we have to make sure we put in a `0`, it seems like things would be simpler if we just appended `{}` for dynamic samplers since `SamplerDesc::asSpan()` already knows how to write just a single int.",
      "parentUuid": "99f23a83_fbdd54bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 262,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 262,
        "endChar": 85
      },
